+## AstroAKD-Bench — local agent benchmark (optional)
+
+**AstroAKD-Bench** is an additive, MCP-native framework for generating
+astronomical archive-discovery questions, validating reference archive
+responses, and recording how an independent AI agent answers the questions
+using this same MCP server. It runs on your laptop against
+`http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp`; existing `server.py` and `executor.py` are unchanged.
+
+The benchmark is maintained separately from the MCP server version. Its
+**current version is 0.4.0**, with local connectivity (0.1.0), synthetic query
+generation (0.2.0), live reference validation (0.3.0), and agent execution/MCP
+tracing (0.4.0). The first three milestones are accepted on the development
+laptop; 0.4.0 passes offline regression tests but still awaits live agent
+qualification. Scientific scoring (0.5.0) and offline replay (0.6.0) are planned.
+
+Start the existing MCP server:
+
+```bash
+uv run fastmcp run server.py --transport http --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
+```
+
+In another terminal, from this repository root:
+
+```bash
+uv run python -m benchmark doctor --smoke
+# With the completed 0.2.0 and 0.3.0 datasets already on disk:
+# No-model harness check ONLY; not a real agent performance measurement:
+uv run python -m benchmark run --agent echo --strict-accepted-020 --limit 5
+```
+
+Use `--agent openai` for optional OpenAI API tool calling, or `--agent external`
+with an importable async adapter for your existing AstroAKD agent. The OpenAI
+option requires a separately supplied API key and SDK; prior benchmark stages
+and the echo harness do **not** require an OpenAI API. Never interpret
+structurally accepted archive responses or completed agent runs as validated
+scientific answer accuracy.
+
+Full instructions: [AstroAKD-Bench guide](docs/benchmark/astroakd_bench.md)
+and [agent tracing](docs/benchmark/agent_execution.md). The **root
+[CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md)** records every AstroAKD-Bench milestone and its
+qualification status.
+
